# Script Scheduler - schedule
#
# Each line starts a script from the "scripts" folder (next to this file):
#
#   minute hour day month weekday  script  [arguments]
#   @boot                          script  [arguments]
#   @boot+N                        script  [arguments]
#
#   minute 0-59, hour 0-23, day 1-31, month 1-12 (or jan-dec),
#   weekday 0-7 (0 and 7 = Sunday, or sun-sat)
#   Allowed are *, lists (1,15), ranges (1-5) and steps (*/10, 0-30/5).
#   @boot starts the script once after the NAS has booted,
#   @boot+N only N minutes after boot (N = 1-1440).
#
# Examples:
#   30 2 * * *     backup.sh            daily at 02:30
#   */15 * * * *   check.sh             every 15 minutes
#   0 6 * * 1-5    report.sh --short    on weekdays at 06:00
#   @boot          setup.sh             after every restart
#   @boot+5        setup.sh             5 minutes after every restart
#
# Lines starting with "#" are comments. "#off " at the start of a line
# disables an entry (the web interface does the same). Changes to this
# file are picked up automatically within a minute.

#off */5 * * * * @EXAMPLE@
